'''''Globularia alypum''''', the '''Alypo globe daisy''' or '''shrubby globularia''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Plantaginaceae]], with a Mediterranean distribution.<ref name="POWO_813050-1" >{{cite POWO |id=813050-1 |title=''Globularia alypum'' L. |access-date=1 May 2023 }}</ref><ref name="commonname" >{{cite web |url=https://identify.plantnet.org/the-plant-list/species/Globularia%20alypum%20L./data |title=''Globularia alypum'' L. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2023 |website=plantnet.org |publisher=Pl@ntNet |access-date=1 May 2023 }}</ref> A shrub that is often co-dominant in the [[calcareous]] shrublands in which it occurs, it is used as a [[purgative]].<ref name="1_of_3810_Google_Scholar_Results" >{{cite journal |title=Contrasting Growth Changes in Two Dominant Species of a Mediterranean Shrubland Submitted to Experimental Drought and Warming |year=2004 |last1=Llorens |first1=L. |last2=Peñuelas |first2=J. |last3=Estiarte |first3=M. |last4=Bruna |first4=P. |journal=Annals of Botany |volume=94 |issue=6 |pages=843–853 |doi=10.1093/aob/mch211 |pmid=15466877 |pmc=4242278 }}</ref><ref name="2_of_3810_Google_Scholar_Results" >{{cite journal |title=Purgative/Laxative actions of ''Globularia alypum'' aqueous extract on gastrointestinal-physiological function and against loperamide-induced constipation coupled to oxidative stress and inflammation in rats |year=2020 |last1=Hajji |first1=Najla |last2=Wannes |first2=Dalanda |last3=Jabri |first3=Mohamed-Amine |last4=Rtibi |first4=Kais |last5=Tounsi |first5=Haifa |last6=Abdellaoui |first6=Afifa |last7=Sebai |first7=Hichem |journal=Neurogastroenterology & Motility |volume=32 |issue=8 |article-number=e13858 |doi=10.1111/nmo.13858 |pmid=32337785 |s2cid=216556560 }}</ref>
